  "source": {
    "source_id": "pbps-v1:isotropic-gaussian-noise-density-prerequisite",
    "anchor": "arXiv:2609.06905v1, Section 2.2, (2.6)-(2.7), selected Gaussian-noise density prerequisite",
    "original_text": "ASTIS mathematical expansion of the standard Gaussian-noise density used in the passage from the independent augmentation (2.7) to the density (2.6), not a quotation or the complete joint-law claim. For a finite-dimensional real inner-product space E with its Borel sigma algebra and canonical inner-product volume, any eta>0, and standard Gaussian G on E, the law of sqrt(eta)*G has volume density ((sqrt(2*pi*eta))^(-1))^dim(E) * exp(-||z||^2/(2*eta)). The natural-power expression also includes dimension zero. This explicitly extends the noise calculation beyond the paper's positive-dimensional Euclidean notation and does not need the sampler's upper bound eta<=1/beta. No potential, input distribution, Gibbs normalizer, conditional law or process conclusion is part of this selected prerequisite. The actual joint augmentation and source Gibbs-density instantiation remain separate proof obligations.",
    "text_sha256": "87dea313eb0698c2bb72e3bff5e7078b46d952ec770e0a6d76656ee480fe3d15"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.IsotropicGaussianDensity.map_sqrt_smul_stdGaussian_eq_withDensity",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Measure/IsotropicGaussianDensity.lean",
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] (η : ℝ), 0 < η → (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E).map (fun z : E => Real.sqrt η • z) = (volume : MeasureTheory.Measure E).withDensity (fun z => ENNReal.ofReal (((Real.sqrt (2 * Real.pi * η))⁻¹) ^ Module.finrank ℝ E * Real.exp (-‖z‖ ^ 2 / (2 * η))))",
    "statement_sha256": "06ba06ee300aa2f0b6280f7b31f6efd6cc328f933616e5d3a7d1d644c74428ab",
    "compiled": true
  },
  "blind_reconstruction": {
    "text": "Let E be any finite-dimensional real inner-product space, with the norm induced by its inner product and with measurable sets equal to the Borel sets of its norm topology. Write d = finrank_ℝ(E) ∈ ℕ. Let γ_E be the centered standard Gaussian probability measure on E with identity covariance, and let λ_E be the canonical Lebesgue measure normalized by orthonormal coordinates. For every real η > 0, the pushforward of γ_E under S_η(z) = √η · z is the following measure on E:\n\n(S_η)_*γ_E = λ_E.withDensity(z ↦ ENNReal.ofReal(((√(2πη))⁻¹)^d · exp(−‖z‖²/(2η)))).\n\nHere pushforward means assigning to a Borel set A the γ_E-measure of S_η⁻¹(A). The measure on the right assigns to A the nonnegative integral of the displayed extended-nonnegative density over A with respect to λ_E. The measure λ_E is the canonical inner-product-space volume, not an arbitrarily chosen measure. Dimension zero is allowed; in that case canonical volume is unit mass on the one-point space, and the exponent d is zero. The exponentiation is natural-number power. The square root is the nonnegative real square root, π is the circle constant, and scalar multiplication is over ℝ. ENNReal.ofReal embeds nonnegative real values and sends negative real values to zero. Real reciprocal and division are totalized at zero, with 0⁻¹ = 0; the assumption η > 0 ensures that the displayed denominators are positive. No separate completeness or nontriviality assumption is imposed.",
    "text_sha256": "e05bf0e5fedd23ee33afadbad8022d765d297ff337b47535e9646bbff039ae12",
    "decoder": "heatbath_exposition_research",
    "decoder_packet_sha256": "28ba97a6fab124287ffb857707dc32a0811e776d107a8c7cd63e68a713f5628d",
    "decoder_run_sha256": "085b561736845cdd6870589378ff8dde4232d033e6420c8ac11ef53a9c350d5f",
